From: firepinn <4785534+firepinn@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rk3506_rproc: probe whether the TCM accepts writes before loading
Upstream-Status: Pending

Loading a new ELF appears to succeed -- rproc_elf_load_segments() returns 0,
remoteproc logs "Booting fw image", the core restarts -- and the firmware that
comes up can still be the previous one, because a write-ignored window returns
no error. Nothing in the load path would say so.

Probe it instead: one word written and read back, with the original restored,
while the core is stopped. The log then says whether a load can mean anything
on this part, rather than leaving it to be deduced from firmware behaviour.

diff --git a/rk3506_rproc.c b/rk3506_rproc.c
index 57eb6e7..58c27c8 100644
--- a/rk3506_rproc.c
+++ b/rk3506_rproc.c
@@ -400,6 +400,47 @@ static void * my_da_to_va(struct rproc * rproc, u64 da, size_t len, bool * is_io
  * the SRAM back, or running the M0 from DDR instead of TCM (see
  * docs/CORTEX-M0.md).
  */
+/*
+ * Does the A7 still own this SRAM?
+ *
+ * Write one word, read it back, put the original back. The core is stopped on
+ * every path that reaches the loader, so the image cannot notice. Returns true
+ * if the window accepted the write.
+ *
+ * This exists because a write-ignored window reports nothing: the load returns
+ * 0, remoteproc logs "Booting fw image", the core restarts, and the previous
+ * firmware comes up. Guessing about that cost a debugging session -- a stale
+ * object file had the firmware reporting an old version number, which looks
+ * exactly like an image that failed to load, and sent the investigation after
+ * the TCM mapping instead of after the build. One line in the log settles it.
+ */
+static bool rk3506_tcm_accepts_writes(struct rproc * rproc)
+{
+  rk3506_mcu_t *  mcu = rproc->priv;
+  u32             saved, probe, readback;
+
+  if (!mcu->tcm_virt)
+    return false;
+
+  saved = readl(mcu->tcm_virt);
+  probe = ~saved;
+
+  writel(probe, mcu->tcm_virt);
+  readback = readl(mcu->tcm_virt);
+  writel(saved, mcu->tcm_virt);
+
+  if (readback != probe)
+  {
+    dev_warn(&rproc->dev,
+             "TCM does not accept writes (wrote 0x%08x, read back 0x%08x): "
+             "the resident image will keep running whatever is loaded",
+             probe, readback);
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  return true;
+}
+
 static int rk3506_rproc_load_once(struct rproc * rproc, const struct firmware * fw)
 {
   rk3506_mcu_t *  mcu = rproc->priv;
@@ -412,6 +453,9 @@ static int rk3506_rproc_load_once(struct rproc * rproc, const struct firmware *
     return 0;
   }
 
+  dev_info(&rproc->dev, "TCM window is %s",
+           rk3506_tcm_accepts_writes(rproc) ? "writable" : "NOT writable");
+
   ret = rproc_elf_load_segments(rproc, fw);
   if (!ret)
     mcu->fw_resident = true;
